s390/alternatives: Allow early alternative patching in decompressor

jira KERNEL-1869
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-741.7.1.el9_9
commit-author Sven Schnelle <svens@linux.ibm.com>
commit 7f9d85998f6c5b989796470fd1ac066232c60723
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-741.7.1.el9_9/7f9d8599.failed

Add the required code to patch alternatives early in the decompressor.
This is required for the upcoming lowcore relocation changes, where
alternatives for facility 193 need to get patched before lowcore
alternatives.

	Reviewed-by: Alexander Gordeev <agordeev@linux.ibm.com>
Co-developed-by: Heiko Carstens <hca@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: Heiko Carstens <hca@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: Sven Schnelle <svens@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: Vasily Gorbik <gor@linux.ibm.com>
(cherry picked from commit 7f9d85998f6c5b989796470fd1ac066232c60723)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

